## Context

One merged hardware boundary, not two: the 5060 Ti 16G (in hand Oct 6)
and the 3975WX (offer 359 EUR sent to atomino206, awaiting answer;
validated band under 400 EUR) go in TOGETHER. CPU swap on the P620 is
~40 min, tool-less, BIOS-native. gpu_inventory extended to CPU and
engine build recorded per run — one HW-v1/HW-v2 boundary in the data.

## Steps

1. CPU + GPU install; 3-GPU topology: A4000+5060Ti as split stages,
   3060 as expert-cache helper (the dev-bench-validated pattern).
2. MANDATORY engine rebuild with archs 86;120 (BUILD.json is [86] only
   today — otherwise "no kernel image"); llama.cpp arch check.
3. Bench --gpu-only-full on the new machine; record.
4. Prefill before/after: the 5060 Ti's 16G restores 8192-token prompt
   chunks (issue #448: the 3060's 512-slot expert cache caps chunks at
   512 tokens, ~350 tok/s prefill). Hypothesis: 1500-3000 tok/s, which
   also cuts the 262K rerun's cold-start from 12.5 min to ~2-3 min.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Both parts in, single boundary recorded (gpu_inventory + BUILD)
- [ ] Rebuild + parity check pass
- [ ] --gpu-only-full bench recorded
- [ ] Prefill before/after measured (the #448 hypothesis tested)
